#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installation"
msgstr "Installacion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid "System Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid "In order to install and use &koffice; you must have:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A functioning &UNIX; system (for example, &Linux; or BSD) with a configured "
"&X-Window; (for example, XFree86 or X.Org)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &Qt; 3.3 libraries from Trolltech. See <ulink url=\"http://www.trolltech."
"com/\">www.trolltech.com</ulink> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The K Desktop Environment 3.3 (&kde; 3.3) or newer. &koffice; cannot be "
"compiled with earlier versions of &kde;. Information on obtaining and "
"installing &kde; can be found at: &kde-http;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Permission to install software on your computer. If you are on a stand-alone "
"system, this should not be a problem. However, if you are using a networked "
"computer, check with your administrator first."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please note that, while you need the &kde; 3.3 (or newer) libraries on your "
"system, you can still use &koffice; in a different desktop environment (for "
"example, XFCE or GNOME)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you plan on <link linkend=\"from-source\">compiling &koffice; from source "
"code</link> you will also need:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:626
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>automake</command> 1.6.1 or later. This can be downloaded from: "
"<ulink url=\"ftp://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/automake/\">ftp://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/"
"automake/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:630
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>autoconf</command> 2.53 or later. This can be downloaded from: "
"<ulink url=\"ftp://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/autoconf/\">ftp://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/"
"autoconf/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A C++ compiler which supports exceptions, preferably a recent version of "
"GCC. (See <ulink url=\"http://gcc.gnu.org\">http://gcc.gnu.org</ulink> for "
"info about getting and installing it.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Troll Tech's &Qt; 3.3 development packages. If these packages are not "
"installed on your system and they are not included in the distribution of "
"your operating system, you should probably have to compile &Qt; from source. "
"These sources can be obtained from <ulink url=\"http://www.trolltech.com/"
"download/index.html\"> http://www.trolltech.com/download/index.html</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:649
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have determined that your system meets these requirements, you "
"should decide whether you want to compile the source code or install from "
"pre-compiled binary packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:655
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to obtain the most current binary version of &koffice;, you can "
"find more information by following this link: <link linkend=\"getting-"
"binaries\">Getting Binary Packages</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:661
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If pre-compiled binaries are not available for your system, you can download "
"the source code and compile it yourself. Instructions on where to obtain the "
"current source code (and what to do with the source code once you have it) "
"can be found by following this link: <link linkend=\"getting-source"
"\">Getting the source code</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please see the <ulink url=\"http://koffice.org\">&koffice; homepage</ulink> "
"for further details. That is where you can always find the most up-to-date "
"information on both source and binary distributions!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:678
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Binary Packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:680
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can download the most current binaries from:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://koffice.org/download"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:689
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or from one of many mirror sites. The current list of mirror sites can be "
"found at:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:695 index.docbook:763
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://www.kde.org/mirrors.html"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:698
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is important that you use a binary package which is compatible with your "
"system. If you use the &Linux; operating system and are unable to find a "
"binary package at the &koffice; web site or one of its mirrors, you may be "
"able to obtain one from the website of your distribution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:708
#, no-c-format
msgid "From Binary Packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:710
#, no-c-format
msgid "To install &koffice; from precompiled binaries, you should:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:716
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Ensure your computer has all of the required software installed and in "
"working condition (excluding &koffice; of course). You can find the system "
"requirements by following this link: <link linkend=\"requirements\">System "
"Requirements</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid "Download the &koffice; binary (or binaries) into a temporary folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the filename ends in <literal role=\"extension\">.rpm</literal> (&RedHat; "
"Package Management file), &koffice; can be installed with the following "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:725
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt><userinput><command>rpm</command><option>-U </"
"option><replaceable>filename</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:727
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the filename ends in <literal role=\"extension\">.deb</literal> (Debian "
"Package file), &koffice; can be installed with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <userinput><command>dpkg</command><option>-i </"
"option><replaceable>filename</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:730
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the filename ends in <literal role=\"extension\">.tar.gz</literal> or "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.tgz</literal> (a tarball file), &koffice; can "
"be installed with the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:733
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <userinput><command>cd</command> /</userinput>\n"
"<prompt>$</prompt> <userinput><command>tar</command> <option>-xzvf</option> "
"<replaceable>filename</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:734
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In these examples <emphasis>filename</emphasis> should be replaced by the "
"complete name of the package <emphasis>including the full path</emphasis> if "
"you are not in the directory in which you saved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:738
#, no-c-format
msgid "That's all. &koffice; should now be installed on your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:743
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have a graphical front-end for package management, such as &kpackage; "
"or <application>GnoRPM</application>, installed on your system, you may find "
"that more convenient to use than a command line. Consult the program's "
"documentation to find out how to install with it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Source Code"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:755
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can download the current source code from: <ulink url=\"http://koffice."
"org/\">http://koffice.org/</ulink> or from one of many mirror sites. The "
"current list of mirror sites can be found at:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:770
#, no-c-format
msgid "From Source Code"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:772
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you want to build &koffice; from source code, you should:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:777
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Ensure your computer has all the required software installed and in working "
"condition (excluding &koffice; of course). You can find the system "
"requirements by following this link: <link linkend=\"requirements\">System "
"Requirements</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:783
#, no-c-format
msgid "Download the &koffice; source file into a temporary folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:786
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the filename ends in <literal role=\"extension\">.src.rpm</literal> "
"(&RedHat; Package Management file), the source code for &koffice; can be "
"installed with:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:790
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <userinput><command>rpm</command><option>-U</option> "
"<replaceable>filename</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:792
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the filename ends in <literal role=\"extension\">.src.tar.gz</literal> or "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.src.tgz</literal> (a tarball file), the source "
"code for &koffice; can be installed with:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:794
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <userinput><command>tar</command> <option>-xzvf</option> "
"<replaceable>filename</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:796
#, no-c-format
msgid "The source code for &koffice; should now be installed on your system."
msgstr ""
